  "summary": "This article begins by describing a moment from Tim Costello's youth when he asked his teacher if poverty is something natural, like the tides or sunrise. His teacher's response shaped his life, and Tim now believes poverty is not natural – it is caused by human decisions and policies. The article paints a picture of him sitting by the beach near his home and reflects on his life's work. Tim, now 69 years old, has spent over 30 years addressing poverty in Australia and traveling to places affected by wars and disasters. He has served as a mayor, written books, and is considered a 'national living treasure' in Australia. Some people confuse him with his brother, Peter Costello, who was a treasurer. Tim, however, is better known as a Baptist minister and was CEO of the charity World Vision for 13 years."
